ate the source of the attack, or preserve evidence for potential legal action. Instant deletion destroys that trail. Quarantine gives them a copy to analyze while keeping the network safe. --- **So, in short:** No detection is absolutely foolproof, and malware is often tangled up with things you need. Quarantining **instantly isolates the threat** (so you’re safe immediately) while keeping your options open. That’s why it’s the smarter, safer default — even when the system is pretty sure it’s caught something bad.
